<h1>Learn how to use Cranium</h1>

<%= link_to "Back", root_path %>

<p>
  Cranium has a pretty hefty list of commands. I'll start out with the basic ones.
</p>

<p>
  At the end, I'll go over the aliases for these commands.
</p>

<h3>
  Install
</h3>

<pre>
  cranium install suomi-lib
</pre>

<h3>Delete</h3>

<pre>
  cranium delete suomi-lib
</pre>

<p>
  Beyond the basics, Cranium offers some nice commands. Here are the rest:
</p>

<h3>Omakase</h3>

<p>
  This provides a list of the top five most popular packages for today
  (refreshes every 24 hours)
</p>

<pre>cranium omakase</pre>

<h3>wipe</h3>

<p>
  This will delete every package you've ever installed with Cranium:
</p>

<pre>cranium wipe</pre>

<p>You can also pass a timeframe using this syntax: older/younger than (x) days</p>

<pre>cranium wipe older than 3 days</pre>

<p>Or,</p>

<pre>cranium wipe younger than 4 days</pre>

<h3>Tear apart</h3>

<p>
  This is used to inspect the source code of a package. <br>
  More specifically, it git clones into the project.
</p>

<pre>cranium tear-apart suomi-lib</pre>

<p>You do not need to have the package installed to do this.</p>

<h3>list</h3>

<p>Provides a list of all your packages</p>

<pre>cranium list</pre>

<p>Like wipe, you can pass a timeframe argument to be more specific:</p>

<pre>cranium list older than 5 days</pre>

<h3>Fun fact</h3>

<p>
  And to top it all off, you can use fun-fact to get a random nordic fun fact:
</p>

<pre>
  cranium fun-fact
</pre>

<h2>TIMTOWTDI</h2>
<p>
  Cranium is a firm believer that there is more than one way to do it. <br>
  For almost every command, there are multiple aliases you can use. Here are all of them: <br>
</p>

<strong>install:</strong>
<ul>
  <li>fetch</li>
  <li>retrieve</li>
  <li>get</li>
  <li>grab</li>
  <li>g</li>
</ul>

<strong>omakase</strong>
<ul>
  <li>menu</li>
</ul>

<strong>massacre</strong>
<ul>
  <li>annihilate</li>
  <li>wipe</li>
</ul>

<strong>delete</strong>
<ul>
  <li>slay</li>
  <li>eradicate</li>
  <li>remove</li>
  <li>execute</li>
</ul>

<strong>list</strong>
<ul>
  <li>my-packages</li>
  <li>packages</li>
</ul>

<p>Anything not mentioned above does not have any aliases.</p>

